From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: publish events across firmware readiness

A udev coldplug trigger can reach Qualcomm battery supplies before GLINK
is ready. Their property getters correctly return EAGAIN; however, the
uevent builder aborts the entire event, losing even supply identity and
type and printing synthetic uevent errors.

Skip temporarily unavailable properties only while composing the event.
Direct sysfs reads retain EAGAIN. Once Qualcomm firmware acknowledges
notification registration, publish a change for each registered supply
so userspace receives the complete initial state even without an unrelated
charger notification. Do not manufacture zero capacity or online values.
Other errors still propagate. This is a local change, not an upstream patch.

Reference: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v7.3-rc5/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
--- a/drivers/power/supply/power_supply_sysfs.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/power_supply_sysfs.c
@@ -543,10 +543,12 @@
 	dev_attr = &pwr_attr->dev_attr;
 
 	ret = power_supply_format_property((struct device *)dev, true, dev_attr, prop_buf);
-	if (ret == -ENODEV || ret == -ENODATA || ret == -EINVAL) {
+	if (ret == -ENODEV || ret == -ENODATA || ret == -EINVAL || ret == -EAGAIN) {
 		/*
 		 * When a battery is absent, we expect -ENODEV. Don't abort;
-		 * send the uevent with at least the PRESENT=0 property
+		 * send the uevent with at least the PRESENT=0 property.
+		 * Firmware-backed supplies can also be temporarily unavailable;
+		 * omit those properties until the driver signals fresh data.
 		 */
 		return 0;
 	}
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1628,8 +1628,20 @@
 	mutex_lock(&battmgr->lock);
 	ret = qcom_battmgr_request(battmgr, &req, sizeof(req));
 	mutex_unlock(&battmgr->lock);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(battmgr->dev, "failed to request power notifications\n");
+		return;
+	}
+
+	/* Replay initial properties that were unavailable before GLINK came up. */
+	if (battmgr->bat_psy)
+		power_supply_changed(battmgr->bat_psy);
+	if (battmgr->usb_psy)
+		power_supply_changed(battmgr->usb_psy);
+	if (battmgr->wls_psy)
+		power_supply_changed(battmgr->wls_psy);
+	if (battmgr->ac_psy)
+		power_supply_changed(battmgr->ac_psy);
 }
 
 static void qcom_battmgr_pdr_notify(void *priv, int state)
